{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rtk rg --files docs && rtk read AGENTS.md'","aggregated_output":"docs/ (10 files)\nindex.md\narchitecture/data-model.md\narchitecture/boundaries.md\narchitecture/contracts.md\narchitecture/stack.md\nglossary.md\nspecs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/spec.md\nbehavior/returns/calculate-refund.md\nbehavior/returns/request-return.md\nbehavior/returns/process-return.md\n# Webshop\n\n<!-- project-memory:start · managed by docs-init; edit outside these markers -->\n## Project memory\n- Start every task at docs/index.md, or at the active spec's tasks.md on a spec\n  branch, and load only what they link to. Load glossary.md when naming things and\n  decisions/ before changing a lasting choice.\n- Answer what the product does from docs/behavior/; open the code only to change it.\n- Every code change belongs to a spec in docs/specs/. None yet: start one (spec-start).\n- One branch per spec, named after its slug. The active spec is the one matching the current branch.\n- Every session adds its line to tasks.md. If something changes mid-way, update spec.md\n  or plan.md, then recheck every task.\n- Write specs, plans, tasks, glossary terms and decisions into docs/,\n  never into SPEC.md, tasks/, CONTEXT.md or docs/superpowers/.\n- Before opening a pull request, ship the spec (spec-ship); the PR title starts with the slug.\n<!-- project-memory:end -->\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rtk read /Users/yousefallaban/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/references/plan.md && rtk read /Users/yousefallaban/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/assets/plan.md'","aggregated_output":"Purpose: section rules for `specs/<id>/plan.md`. Template: `assets/plan.md`.\n\nFrontmatter: `spec`, the spec id.\n\nApproach: required. The shape of the solution in 3 to 8 lines. Don't restate the why.\n\nTrade-offs: optional, when there was a real choice. The options considered and why this one won. A choice that outlives the spec links to its decision record. Not every idea mentioned in passing.\n\nFiles: required. The annotated file tree: path, new or changed or deleted, one-line reason. This is the scope the review checks the diff against, and the list spec-build asks before leaving. Not line-level edits.\n\nArchitecture to update at ship: optional, when an architecture area changes. Each area file and the reference file it comes from. spec-ship updates exactly these. Not the content itself.\n\nRollout: optional, only when order matters. Migrations, flags, deploy order, backfills. Not standard deploy steps.\n\nRisks: optional. What could break and which claim or test covers it. Not generic risks.\n\nA plan past about 60 lines means the change is too big, or design detail belongs in reference/.\n---\nspec: \"{{spec id}}\"\n---\n## Approach\n<!-- required: the shape of the solution, in 3 to 8 lines. Don't restate the why. -->\n\n## Trade-offs\n<!-- optional: when there was a real choice. Options considered and why this one won.\nA choice that outlives the spec links to its decision record. -->\n\n## Files\n<!-- required: the annotated file tree. This is the scope the review checks the diff against. -->\n{{path}}    {{new | changed | deleted}}: {{one-line reason}}\n\n## Architecture to update at ship\n<!-- optional: when an architecture area changes. spec-ship updates exactly these files,\neach from the reference file it names. -->\n- {{area}}.md, from reference/{{file}}\n\n## Rollout\n<!-- optional: only when order matters. Migrations, feature flags, deploy order, data backfills. -->\n\n## Risks\n<!-- optional: what could break, and which claim or test covers it. -->\n\n<!-- A plan past about 60 lines means the change is too big, or design detail belongs in reference/. -->\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
