{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rtk read /Users/yousefallaban/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/references/reference.md && rtk read /Users/yousefallaban/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/references/decision.md && rtk read /Users/yousefallaban/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/assets/decision.md'","aggregated_output":"Purpose: rules for `specs/<id>/reference/*`. No template.\n\nFree format. The first line says what the file is: `Purpose: ...`. Data model sketches, contract drafts, API examples, research, mockups: anything the spec needs while it is being planned and built.\n\nNever the why, the plan or progress; those live in spec.md, plan.md and tasks.md. A reference file is not edited at ship; the architecture files plan.md lists are updated from it, and the reference file stays as the record of the draft.\nPurpose: rules for `decisions/<date>-<slug>.md`. Template: `assets/decision.md`.\n\nFrontmatter: `id` as YYYY-MM-DD-slug; `status`, accepted or `superseded by <id>`; `spec`, the spec it came from; `date`.\n\nTitle: the decision as a short statement, such as \"Store wishlists on the server\".\n\nContext: the forces that made a choice necessary, in 2 to 5 lines. Options: each option in one line, with why it lost or won. Decision: one sentence. Consequences: what gets easier, what gets harder, what to watch.\n\nA decision is written the moment a lasting choice is made, during grilling, planning or building. It is never edited once accepted. A new decision supersedes it, and only the old one's status changes. Agents read accepted decisions only. Step-by-step detail belongs in plan.md or reference/.\n---\nid: \"{{YYYY-MM-DD-slug}}\"\nstatus: accepted\nspec: \"{{spec id}}\"\ndate: \"{{YYYY-MM-DD}}\"\n---\n# {{The decision as a short statement}}\n\n## Context\n<!-- the forces that made a choice necessary, in 2 to 5 lines -->\n\n## Options\n- {{option}}: {{why it lost, or why it won}}\n\n## Decision\n{{one sentence}}\n\n## Consequences\n<!-- what gets easier, what gets harder, what to watch -->\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
