{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rtk read docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/spec.md'","aggregated_output":"---\nid: 2026-10-13-customer-wishlist\nkind: feature\nstatus: draft\nsummary: Customers can save catalogue products to a wishlist and view or remove them.\nrequest: Customers can save items to a wishlist.\napproved: {by: Sanne, via: in session}\n---\n# Save items to a wishlist\n\n## Why\n\nCustomers can lose track of products they are interested in but are not ready to buy.\nFinding those products again takes effort, and customers may never return to complete the purchase.\nSuccess means customers return to saved products and those saved products turn into orders.\n\n## What changes\n\n### Add · wishlist/save-items\n\n- Callers can save any catalogue product to a wishlist using a supplied `customerId` string. {#save-item}\n  e.g. A caller saves a headlamp for customer-1 -> the headlamp is included in customer-1's wishlist.\n\n- Callers use one wishlist per `customerId` without signing in or creating a customer record. {#customer-id-wishlist}\n  e.g. A caller saves a headlamp and then a tent for customer-1 without signing in -> both products belong to the same customer-1 wishlist.\n\n- Callers save products without quantities. {#product-only-items}\n  e.g. A caller saves a headlamp -> the saved item represents the headlamp product without a quantity.\n\n- Callers receive an error when saving a product ID that is absent from the catalogue. {#reject-unknown-product}\n  e.g. A caller tries to save a product ID that the catalogue does not contain -> saving fails with an error.\n\n- Callers leave the wishlist unchanged when saving a product already on it, retaining one entry and its original save moment. {#preserve-first-save}\n  e.g. A caller saves a headlamp at 10:00, a tent at 10:05 and the headlamp again at 10:10 -> the headlamp remains one entry saved at 10:00, behind the tent.\n\n### Add · wishlist/view-items\n\n- Callers see only the saved products associated with the `customerId` they supply. {#isolate-wishlists}\n  e.g. Customer-1 has saved a headlamp and customer-2 has saved a tent -> viewing customer-2's wishlist shows only the tent.\n\n- Callers see each saved product with its name and the price the catalogue currently holds. {#current-product-details}\n  e.g. A headlamp was saved when its catalogue price was 3000 cents, and the catalogue now lists it at 3500 cents -> the wishlist shows the headlamp's name and 3500 cents.\n\n- Callers see saved products ordered from most recently saved to least recently saved. {#newest-first}\n  e.g. A headlamp was saved at 10:00 and a tent at 10:05 -> viewing the wishlist returns the tent before the headlamp.\n\n- Callers receive an empty list when the supplied `customerId` has no saved products. {#empty-list}\n  e.g. Customer-1 has no saved products -> viewing customer-1's wishlist returns an empty list without an error.\n\n### Add · wishlist/remove-items\n\n- Callers can remove a saved product from the wishlist identified by the supplied `customerId`. {#remove-item}\n  e.g. A caller removes the headlamp saved for customer-1 -> the headlamp no longer appears in customer-1's wishlist.\n\n- Callers receive an error when removing a product that is not on the addressed wishlist. {#reject-unsaved-product}\n  e.g. Customer-1 has saved only a tent, and a caller tries to remove a headlamp from that wishlist -> removal fails with an error.\n\n- Callers leave other customers' wishlists unchanged when removing a saved product. {#isolate-removal}\n  e.g. Customer-1 and customer-2 both saved a headlamp, and a caller removes it for customer-1 -> customer-2's wishlist still contains the headlamp.\n\n## Not doing\n\n- Sign-in or a new customer entity.\n- Buying from the wishlist; that belongs to a separate spec.\n- Sharing wishlists, named lists or multiple lists per customer.\n- Price or stock alerts.\n- Quantities or price snapshots on saved items.\n- Stock handling or behavior for products becoming unavailable or disappearing from the catalogue; the catalogue is currently fixed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
