{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rtk read docs/architecture/stack.md && rtk read docs/architecture/data-model.md && rtk read docs/architecture/boundaries.md && rtk read docs/architecture/contracts.md'","aggregated_output":"---\narea: stack\n---\n# Stack\n\n## Languages and frameworks\n\n| Name | Version | Used for |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| TypeScript | Not pinned | Returns functions and types in `src/returns.ts`; shared order types in `src/orders.ts` |\n| Bun | Not pinned | Running the returns tests with `bun:test` |\n\n## Commands\n\n| Task | Command |\n| --- | --- |\n| Test | `bun test` |\n---\narea: data-model\n---\n# Data model\n\n| Entity | Key fields | Relations |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `Return` | `id` (string, generated as `return-N` using a module-local counter), `orderId`, `items`, `refundCents` (number of cents), `status` (`requested`, `approved` or `refunded`), `requestedAt` (`Date`) | In-memory value defined in `src/returns.ts`; `orderId` references the supplied `Order.id`; embeds `ReturnItem[]` |\n| `ReturnItem` | `productId` (string), `quantity` (number) | Embedded in `Return.items`; product lookup uses the first matching `Order.lines` entry |\n| `Order` (returns input) | Returns reads `id`, `lines`, `discountPercent`, `status` and optional `deliveredAt` (`Date`) | Type defined in `src/orders.ts`; supplies `OrderLine[]` to the returns module |\n| `OrderLine` (returns input) | `productId`, `quantity`, `unitPriceCents` | Embedded in `Order.lines`; provides the recorded price and quantity for a matching `ReturnItem` |\n---\narea: boundaries\n---\n# Boundaries\n\n| Module | Path | Domain | May depend on |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Returns | `src/returns.ts` (re-exported by `src/index.ts`); tests in `test/returns.test.ts` | returns | `Order` from `src/orders.ts` through a type-only import; JavaScript built-ins for dates, arithmetic and collections |\n---\narea: contracts\n---\n# Contracts\n\n| Name | Kind | Input | Output | Consumers |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `calculateRefund` | Exported synchronous TypeScript function in `src/returns.ts` | `order: Order`, `items: ReturnItem[]` | Number of cents from `Math.round(subtotal * (1 - order.discountPercent / 100))`, where subtotal sums each entry's quantity times its first matching order line's unit price; throws `Error` for an unmatched product; performs no quantity or delivery validation | `submitReturn`; re-exported by `src/index.ts` |\n| `submitReturn` | Exported synchronous TypeScript function in `src/returns.ts` | `order: Order`, `items: ReturnItem[]`, optional `now: Date` (defaults to the current time) | New `Return` with copied item entries, the calculated amount and requested status; throws `Error` on validation failure; accepts supplied values without a return-history store | `test/returns.test.ts`; re-exported by `src/index.ts` |\n| `approveReturn` | Exported synchronous TypeScript function in `src/returns.ts` | `ret: Return` | New top-level `Return` value with approved status; throws `Error` unless the input status is requested | `test/returns.test.ts`; re-exported by `src/index.ts` |\n| `refundReturn` | Exported synchronous TypeScript function in `src/returns.ts` | `ret: Return` | New top-level `Return` value with refunded status; throws `Error` unless the input status is approved; performs no payment-service call | `test/returns.test.ts`; re-exported by `src/index.ts` |\n| `RETURN_WINDOW_DAYS` | Exported numeric constant in `src/returns.ts` | Read access | `30`, fixed in source; used with a day length of 86,400,000 milliseconds | `submitReturn`; re-exported by `src/index.ts` |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
